# Intermediate binding 'b' is introduced by a body dict but never referenced
# from the final expression — the lost-binding warning fires.
# The intermediate dict [b: [+ b 2]] creates a new binding 'b' that shadows the param 'b'.
# The final expression [if a 1 0] uses 'a' but not the intermediate 'b', so it is lost.
[call [fn [let a b] [b: [+ b 2]] [if a 1 0]] 1 2]
=== out
Int(1)

=== warn
variable 'b' is never referenced
